{"file":"cloudflare/control-plane/src/index.js","line":147,"rule":"Correctness / Security","severity":"high","message":"HOSTNAME_PATTERN is case-insensitive and the hostname is bound without lowercasing. SQLite `=` and the unique index are case-sensitive, so attaching 'Foo.Example.com' bypasses the collision check and the unique index for a hostname another tenant holds as 'foo.example.com'. DNS hostnames are case-insensitive, so the cross-tenant collision this commit sets out to prevent is still possible. Normalize the hostname to lowercase before the check and the insert, or use COLLATE NOCASE."}
{"file":"cloudflare/control-plane/src/index.js","line":155,"rule":"Correctness (concurrency, error handling)","severity":"medium","message":"The collision check, addCustomHostname and the UPDATE are not atomic. Two concurrent attach requests can both pass the check. The loser's UPDATE then throws a unique-constraint error, which becomes an unhandled 500 after the external addCustomHostname call has already run, leaving an orphaned custom hostname. Catch the constraint violation, map it to 409 and roll back the external call."}
{"file":"cloudflare/control-plane/src/index.js","line":142,"rule":"Code Comments","severity":"low","message":"The comment says resolveTenant's lookup 'has no ORDER BY guarantee', but this same commit adds ORDER BY id to that lookup. The comment is stale and misleading."}
{"file":"cloudflare/control-plane/schema.sql","line":12,"rule":"Maintainability / Performance","severity":"low","message":"The new unique index uniq_tenants_subdomain duplicates the existing non-unique idx_tenants_subdomain on the same column. This adds redundant write overhead and storage. Replace the old index instead of adding a second one."}
{"file":"cloudflare/control-plane/migrations/0002-add-hostname-uniqueness.sql","line":7,"rule":"Correctness","severity":"low","message":"The migration creates unique indexes with no pre-check or handling for existing duplicate rows. Production data that already collides makes the migration fail. Also, the unique index only covers custom_hostname, so a custom_hostname equal to another tenant's subdomain is still allowed at the DB level. The defense-in-depth claim therefore holds only partially."}
{"file":"cloudflare/control-plane/src/index.js","line":136,"rule":"Test Coverage","severity":"medium","message":"The commit adds a 409 conflict path, the ORDER BY id lookup and two unique indexes, but no tests. Missing cases include a collision with another tenant's subdomain, a collision with another tenant's custom_hostname, re-attaching the same hostname to the same tenant (the id != ?2 exclusion), a case-variant hostname, and deterministic resolution in the delivery worker."}
